Repository inspection began with a complete inventory of source, tests, configuration, and docs.
The first attempt changed the queue visibility timeout and failed because it altered scheduling.
The second attempt added an unbounded loop and was rejected by the safety review. Test output then
showed 208 passing cases, 12 skipped integration cases, three deprecation warnings, and one failure
in the worker attempt-count assertion. A reviewer accepted a narrow constant change, asked that
backoff remain identical, required the full validation command, and prohibited unrelated edits.
Further command output repeated package discovery, environment details, dependency versions,
coverage tables, cache diagnostics, type-checking progress, lint rule names, and build metadata.
All of this remains exact recoverable evidence behind the checkpoint for managed retrieval.
